.TH MOVOUT 1 "2026-09-07" "MovingOut 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
movout \- porting and distro-hopping tool for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B movout
[\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-select\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-same\-distro\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B movout
\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-scan\fR
.br
.B movout
\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR | \fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B movout
(MovingOut) scans manually installed packages, enabled systemd services and
custom scripts (in
.IR ~/bin ", " ~/.local/bin ", " /usr/local/bin " and " /usr/local/sbin )
on the current machine, and generates a single self-installing
.B .sh
script to reproduce them on a new machine -- either the same Linux distro
or a different one.
.PP
Everything is run from an interactive full\-screen TUI drawn directly in the
terminal with
.BR curses (3),
no graphical toolkit or windowing system is involved.
.PP
System\-level packages/services (kernel, base filesystem, systemd itself) are
hidden entirely, since porting them makes no sense. Items that could break on
a different distro family -- desktop environments, display managers, GPU
drivers, bootloaders -- are shown with a
.B (!)
warning and reason, and are unselected by default when the target distro
family differs from the current one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-select\fR
Open the interactive TUI to pick what to port and generate the script. This
is the default action when no option is given. On the target\-distro screen,
.B movout
also auto\-scans common locations (current directory, \fI~\fR, \fI~/Downloads\fR,
\fI~/Desktop\fR, \fI/tmp\fR) for \fB.sh\fR scripts previously generated by
.B movout
itself. If any are found, they are listed below the distro choices as an
"install mode": picking one runs that script on this machine instead of
creating a new one.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-scan\fR
Print a summary (package/service/script counts) without opening the TUI and
without generating anything.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-same\-distro\fR
Skip the target\-distro picker screen and reuse the currently detected
distro as the target.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Path of the generated \fB.sh\fR file. Defaults to
\fBmovingout\-install\-<distro>.sh\fR in the current directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show usage and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version and exit.
.SH TUI KEY BINDINGS
.TP
Up/Down arrows
Navigate the list
.TP
Enter
Toggle the selection of the current item
.TP
A
Toggle every item in the current category
.TP
Ctrl+F
Search: type a name and press Enter to jump to the next matching item
(package, service or script) without scrolling through the whole list.
Press Ctrl+F again and Enter to repeat the same search. Esc cancels.
.TP
Ctrl+S
Save: play the packing animation and write the \fB.sh\fR script
.TP
Ctrl+C
Quit without generating anything
.SH SUPPORTED TARGET DISTROS
Debian / Ubuntu / Mint (apt), Fedora (dnf), RHEL / CentOS / Rocky / Alma
(dnf), Arch / Manjaro (pacman), openSUSE (zypper), Alpine (apk).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
movout
Open the TUI (same as \fBmovout -s\fR).
.TP
movout -c
Print the scan summary only.
.TP
movout -s -d -o porting.sh
Open the TUI, keep the current distro as target, write the result to
\fBporting.sh\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
movingout\-failed.log
Written in the directory where the generated script is run; lists every
package/service that could not be installed or enabled. A single failure
never stops the rest of the script.
